  "notes": "A compound of {渡|と} (to cross over) and {米|べい} (America, from {米国|べいこく}). This pattern exists for other countries:\n\n- {渡英|とえい} — going to England\n- {渡仏|とふつ} — going to France\n- {渡独|とどく} — going to Germany\n- {渡欧|とおう} — going to Europe\n\nThese compounds are more concise and slightly more formal than saying アメリカに{行|い}く. They are commonly used in news, biographies, and formal writing.",
